<p class=MsoNormal><a name=fn1></a><span style='mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
color:black'>1. The sample is selected from among the largest banks in each
Federal Reserve District. In the table, large banks are defined as those with total
domestic assets of $20 billion or more as of June 30, 2016. The combined assets
of the 39 large banks totaled $9.6 trillion, compared to $9.8 trillion for the
entire panel of 69 banks, and 13.9 trillion for all domestically chartered,
federally insured commercial banks. <o:p></o:p></span></p>

